SoapyAirspyHF: report the device's errors, and the settings it accepted

The module ignored libairspyhf's result for every setting it writes, and
updated what it reports before the write:

- setFrequency() kept the new frequency and ignored airspyhf_set_freq(),
  so a refused tune left the device on the old channel while
  getFrequency() reported the new one.
- setSampleRate() only kept the request, and getSampleRate() returned it.
  activateStream() and a read with a rate change pending wrote it later
  and ignored both airspyhf_set_samplerate() and airspyhf_start():
  activateStream() returned success for a stream that never started, or
  that ran at the old rate.
- setGain() and setGainMode() kept the new attenuator, LNA or AGC setting
  and ignored the write, and the open ignored its LNA and AGC writes.

Each write is now checked, and what the module reports changes only once
the device has taken it. A refused setting throws std::runtime_error, which
SoapySDR's C API turns into an error code. setSampleRate() writes the rate
at once, so getSampleRate() returns a rate the device accepted; on a
running stream it stops, writes and restarts, as a pending rate did, and a
refused rate leaves the stream running on the rate it had.
activateStream() and a read that applies a pending rate return
SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR when the rate write or the start fails, and the
rate stays pending. An open whose LNA or AGC write fails after the
attenuator answered closes the device and throws.

dsd-neo applies this patch to the SoapyAirspyHF module it builds for its
Windows release.

Generated against SoapyAirspyHF 0b3daf0b47c3c1d0857c873bb184f6a86a37333c.

